1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
You've walked your act alone.

2
00:00:02,624 --> 00:00:04,363
You know it works.

3
00:00:06,163 --> 00:00:10,076
What you don't know is how long it takes,

4
00:00:10,526 --> 00:00:14,874
what a crew does when they don't know the answers,

5
00:00:15,324 --> 00:00:18,367
or which of your sentences nobody understood.

6
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:23,211
Today you find out, with real people.

7
00:00:24,111 --> 00:00:28,024
And then you read what the game wrote down,

8
00:00:28,474 --> 00:00:31,952
and you change three things, and only three.

9
00:00:33,152 --> 00:00:35,326
Three checks before anybody arrives.

10
00:00:35,776 --> 00:00:38,385
Each sees something the others can't.

11
00:00:40,185 --> 00:00:41,924
The first is lint.

12
00:00:42,824 --> 00:00:45,867
If it isn't clean, you're not ready.

13
00:00:47,067 --> 00:00:49,676
The second is the printed bible.

14
00:00:50,576 --> 00:00:52,315
Go down the beats,

15
00:00:52,765 --> 00:00:56,243
and read only two lines under each step.

16
00:00:56,693 --> 00:00:58,867
Reached from, and leads to.

17
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:06,320
The first step leads somewhere, and is reached from nowhere, and that's right.

18
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:11,133
Every later step is reached from the one before.

19
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:15,511
And the act's ending leads nowhere, for now.

20
00:01:17,311 --> 00:01:24,267
If a later step is sitting up in the first beat, with no reached from line,

21
00:01:24,717 --> 00:01:29,500
then nothing reveals it, and no crew will ever see it.

22
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,309
The third check is the walk.

23
00:01:34,209 --> 00:01:38,991
You go down the spine alone, as fast as you can.

24
00:01:40,791 --> 00:01:43,400
And then you delete the save.

25
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:46,909
This is the one people forget.

26
00:01:47,809 --> 00:01:49,548
I'd forget it too,

27
00:01:49,998 --> 00:01:53,476
so it's written on the page in bold.

28
00:01:55,276 --> 00:02:00,059
A crew that sits down to a save you've walked through

29
00:02:00,509 --> 00:02:03,552
starts at the end of your act.

30
00:02:04,752 --> 00:02:06,491
Now for the people.

31
00:02:06,941 --> 00:02:11,289
There are five rules, and they're harder than they look.

32
00:02:12,189 --> 00:02:16,537
Say what the game is, and nothing about the story.

33
00:02:17,437 --> 00:02:20,046
Don't answer questions. Write them down.

34
00:02:20,946 --> 00:02:24,859
Where do we go, isn't a question for you.

35
00:02:25,309 --> 00:02:28,352
It's a lead that didn't say where.

36
00:02:30,152 --> 00:02:33,630
Write the time whenever a step shows done.

37
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:38,039
Don't stop them leaving the spine.

38
00:02:38,489 --> 00:02:41,098
If they take three jobs instead,

39
00:02:41,548 --> 00:02:45,026
that's the best thing you'll learn all week.

40
00:02:46,826 --> 00:02:48,565
And end it yourself.

41
00:02:49,765 --> 00:02:53,678
When they've gone, look at what the game recorded.

42
00:02:55,478 --> 00:02:58,087
The runtime log should be empty.

43
00:02:59,887 --> 00:03:01,626
Then open the save.

44
00:03:02,076 --> 00:03:04,250
Don't change it. Just read.

45
00:03:06,050 --> 00:03:11,702
Under the ship's name is what the ship has earned with each side.

46
00:03:12,602 --> 00:03:14,341
Below that, the credits.

47
00:03:16,141 --> 00:03:19,185
And then every step of your story,

48
00:03:19,635 --> 00:03:21,374
each with a state.

49
00:03:22,274 --> 00:03:25,317
One is open, and two is hidden.

50
00:03:25,767 --> 00:03:27,507
Ninety-nine means it's done.

51
00:03:28,407 --> 00:03:30,580
Now search for state one.

52
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:35,393
There should be exactly one step of your spine.

53
00:03:35,843 --> 00:03:39,757
That's the hook, and that's where next week begins.

54
00:03:40,957 --> 00:03:44,435
Before you close that folder, copy the file.

55
00:03:45,335 --> 00:03:47,509
Name it for the evening.

56
00:03:49,309 --> 00:03:52,787
The start screen has a new game choice

57
00:03:53,237 --> 00:03:55,846
that replaces the save without asking.

58
00:03:56,746 --> 00:04:01,528
A copy every week is the only undo a campaign has.

59
00:04:03,328 --> 00:04:05,502
And remember what's in it.

60
00:04:05,952 --> 00:04:08,561
Every hidden step, word for word.

61
00:04:09,461 --> 00:04:12,939
So keep it where the crew doesn't look.

62
00:04:14,139 --> 00:04:17,183
Now compare your notes with your plan,

63
00:04:17,633 --> 00:04:20,241
and write three changes. No more.

64
00:04:21,141 --> 00:04:26,359
More than three, and you can't tell next week which one helped.

65
00:04:28,159 --> 00:04:30,767
The commonest first one is this.

66
00:04:31,217 --> 00:04:36,000
The crew arrives, and somebody asks, what do we do now?

67
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,539
A description is atmosphere.

68
00:04:40,439 --> 00:04:45,657
So give the step an order, on a line of its own.

69
00:04:46,557 --> 00:04:49,165
And name the console in it.

70
00:04:50,965 --> 00:04:53,139
Scan the Wren from Science.

71
00:04:54,039 --> 00:04:57,083
That's the cheapest fix in this class.

72
00:04:58,283 --> 00:05:00,022
Lint still says clean.

73
00:05:00,922 --> 00:05:02,661
So delete the save,

74
00:05:03,111 --> 00:05:07,459
and play it again with different people if you can.

75
00:05:09,259 --> 00:05:11,867
A crew that's seen evening one

76
00:05:12,317 --> 00:05:15,796
can't tell you if the new order helps.

77
00:05:17,596 --> 00:05:22,378
Every playtest of an evening needs people who haven't seen it.

78
00:05:23,278 --> 00:05:28,061
So save your friends for the evenings you're least sure of.

79
00:05:29,261 --> 00:05:34,043
So a walk proves the steps are joined, and nothing else.

80
00:05:35,843 --> 00:05:38,017
The game records what happened,

81
00:05:38,467 --> 00:05:41,076
and only your notes say why.

82
00:05:42,876 --> 00:05:47,224
So make three changes, keep a copy of the save,

83
00:05:47,674 --> 00:05:50,283
and then write the next evening.
